    <string name="about_what">What this is</string>
    <string name="about_blurb">A home screen made of blocks you choose, arrange and restyle. Every page, every block and every setting lives in this app\'s own storage on this phone.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy">Where your things go</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_body">Nowhere. Nulis does not declare the internet permission, so Android will not let it open a connection even if it tried to. There is no analytics and no crash reporting.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_check">You can check that yourself: adb shell dumpsys package %1$s lists every permission it holds.</string>
